--- a/a/README.txt
+++ b/b/README.txt
@@ -1,21 +1,14 @@
-﻿HUYMAIER CONSOLE FSE v0.25.3
+HUYMAIER CONSOLE FSE v0.25.6
 
-- Epic installs/updates now stream Legendary progress into Downloads: percentage, ETA, downloaded/total bytes, and live transfer rate.
-Focused stabilization candidate on top of v0.25.1.
+Controller-first Windows 11 full-screen console shell.
 
-Primary fixes:
-- Windows Update and Driver Updates now have real Settings-owned pages. Opening either page starts a visible scan; results, install actions, errors, and restart-required actions stay on that page.
-- Quick Access location opens a centered Bottom / Top / Left / Right chooser rather than a dead/cycling setting.
-- Controller input owns navigation while active. A stationary mouse no longer steals selection when scrolling moves controls underneath it; physical mouse movement/click restores mouse control.
-- PS/Guide opens Huymaier Quick Access globally, including native PlayStation-family console interfaces; Options remains local to the native console.
-- Downloads history contains only genuine completed install/download events, retained for seven days and capped at twenty. Old Refresh/scan history is removed. Recent direct-provider installs can be reconstructed from provider logs.
-- Apps aggressively excludes recognized games rather than mirroring every Windows Start registration.
-- Epic filtering now rejects Unreal Engine Marketplace assets/plugins/content in local manifests and direct owned-library catalogs, and v0.25.2 forces one cleanup library rescan.
+This stabilization build adds reliable centered option choosers for Quick Access location, keyboard theme, button prompts, music theme, and Windows display scale. Display Scale is under Settings -> Display and uses percentage choices from 100% through 500%; Windows sign-out is surfaced when required for the new account scale to apply fully.
 
-Preserved confirmed behavior:
-- RPCS3 users/profiles work.
-- Steam games populate natively.
-- Shelf uses Library artwork.
-- Emulator platform cards continue direct native-console entry.
+It also preserves the v0.25.5 clean-install startup fix, Epic/Legendary live transfer telemetry, 7-day / 20-entry download history, dedicated Windows Update and Driver Update pages, GitHub self-update, Steam population, RPCS3 users, and shared Shelf/Library artwork.
 
-See RELEASE_NOTES-v0.25.3.txt and Docs\TEST-CHECKLIST.txt.
+Install
+1. Extract the ZIP to a normal local folder such as C:\HC256.
+2. Run Install-HuymaierConsole.cmd.
+3. Launch Huymaier Console from the installed shortcut.
+
+See RELEASE_NOTES-v0.25.6.txt and Docs\TEST-CHECKLIST.txt.
diff --git a/b/RELEASE_NOTES-v0.25.5.txt b/b/RELEASE_NOTES-v0.25.5.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..617f396
--- /dev/null
+++ b/b/RELEASE_NOTES-v0.25.5.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+Huymaier Console v0.25.5
+
+Fresh-PC startup stabilization
+
+- Fixed a first-run crash under PowerShell StrictMode when Home rails were empty. Empty arrays could be unwrapped to $null at function parameter boundaries and then fail on .Count.
+- Home, game-hub, and provider rails now normalize zero/one/many item inputs into stable arrays before Count/index operations.
+- Persisted config list fields are normalized after loading so empty, scalar, and array JSON representations behave identically.
+- Home Random Picks now normalizes the installed-game Entries collection before Count/Get-Random.
+- Fatal startup logs now include InvocationInfo position and ScriptStackTrace when available, making future machine-specific startup failures line-addressable.
+- All v0.25.4 GitHub updater, Epic live telemetry, Downloads retention, Settings update pages, Quick Access, artwork, Steam and RPCS3 fixes are preserved.
diff --git a/b/RELEASE_NOTES-v0.25.6.txt b/b/RELEASE_NOTES-v0.25.6.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d099768
--- /dev/null
+++ b/b/RELEASE_NOTES-v0.25.6.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+Huymaier Console v0.25.6 — Settings Chooser + Windows Scale Stabilization
+
+Changes
+- Fixes the centered choice-popup system under PowerShell StrictMode by explicitly initializing popup state before first use.
+- Quick Access location now reliably opens a centered Bottom / Top / Left / Right chooser.
+- Keyboard Theme now opens a centered Huymaier / Light / High Contrast chooser instead of calling the old cycle action.
+- Button Prompts now use a centered Auto / Xbox / PlayStation / Nintendo / Steam / Keyboard chooser.
+- Music Theme now uses a centered chooser and only offers Custom when a custom music file is configured.
+- Adds Display -> Scale as a percentage-based Windows setting with a centered chooser.
+- Display Scale writes the Windows account DPI scale setting from 100%-500% and reports when Windows sign-out is required for the selected value to apply fully.
+- When a new scale is pending, Display offers a controller-friendly Sign out to apply display scale action with confirmation.
+- Preserves the v0.25.5 fresh-PC empty-collection startup fix and richer fatal startup diagnostics.
+- Preserves Epic/Legendary live download telemetry, 7-day/20-entry download history, GitHub self-update, Windows Update, Driver Updates, Steam population, RPCS3 users, and shared Shelf/Library artwork.
+
+Testing focus
+1. Settings -> Huymaier Console -> Quick Access location: centered popup appears and all four locations are visible at once.
+2. Settings -> Huymaier Console -> Keyboard theme: centered popup appears; selection updates the native keyboard palette.
+3. Button Prompts and Music Theme use the same chooser behavior.
+4. Settings -> Display -> Scale: chooser opens, selected percentage is written, and the page reports current -> configured scale until Windows sign-out.
+5. Sign out action requires confirmation.
+6. Fresh/empty profile still boots without .Count failures.
